Project spy-mocking convention (`.cursor/rules/spy-mocking.mdc`) requires `vi.mock('module', { spy: true })` at the top level and `vi.fn()` / `mockImplementation` calls placed inside `beforeEach` — never inside factory bodies. Lines 11, 14, 20, 28, and 31 all place `vi.fn()` (or `vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(...)`) directly in the factory. The agent modules can be imported without side effects (no API calls happen at module scope), so `{ spy: true }` is viable. Replace, for example:
```ts
vi.mock('./agents/claude-code', { spy: true });
// in beforeEach:
vi.mocked(claudeAgent.execute).mockResolvedValue({ cost: 0.42, ... });
```
